// Look texts with inner voices for the cookhouse and the commander's chamber. A look_<hotspot>
// knot replaces the hotspot's static text, so each repeats it before the voices speak.

=== look_pot_rack ===
Four pots, a pan with a handle too long for any hearth in this garrison, two ladles and a string of sausages that the cook counts every morning. The onions are counted too. Hedda is careful with anything that can be eaten.
-> END

=== look_cat_seat ===
A plaited basket in the warm gap between hearth and oven, with half a sack folded into it and a dent in the middle the size of a curled-up cat. The bowl beside it is red clay and filled every evening.
The milk is fresh. She feeds the cat before she feeds eleven men, and she would deny it under oath. # skill:empathy # passive:8 # line:skill_16
-> END

=== look_ledgers ===
The muster roll and the stores book, side by side. The roll has forty lines ruled in it, and eleven have a name. Under a river stone beside them lies a letter with a crown seal, a month old and unanswered.
A month. He knew something was coming long before Tam rode in, and chose not to open the door to it. # skill:logic # passive:10 # line:skill_17
-> END

=== look_map ===
The march painted on a board: the north road as one red line, the river as a blue one, the garrison a black tower where they nearly cross. Pin holes run along the road, one for every rider that came through.
Where road meets river there is a ford, and somebody has pressed a thumbnail into the paint there until the board split. # skill:perception # passive:9 # line:skill_18
-> END

=== look_shrine ===
A niche no bigger than a loaf, a carved saint in it and an oil lamp that is never let go out. The saint's face is rubbed smooth by thumbs.
The niche is older than the tower. Somebody built a soldier's house around a prayer, and the stone has kept it. # skill:stonework # passive:9 # line:skill_19
-> END

=== look_window ===
A paired window, deep enough to sit in, a shutter folded back on each side. Outside there is nothing: the rock falls away into a valley full of mist and rain.
Ten metres of dark air. Your stomach notices before you do. Breathe out. Step back. # skill:composure # passive:8 # line:skill_20
-> END
